%% section: Write and read paths
%% caption: Write path and read path
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as Client
    participant Co as Coordinator
    participant CL as Commit log
    participant MT as Memtable
    participant SS as SSTables
    C->>Co: write at consistency level
    Co->>CL: append durably
    Co->>MT: apply in memory
    Co-->>C: ack once CL replicas respond
    MT->>SS: flush when full — immutable from here
    C->>Co: read
    Co->>MT: check memtable
    Co->>SS: check each SSTable via bloom filter
    Note over SS: a row spread across many SSTables makes reads slower — that is what compaction fixes
    Co-->>C: merged latest-timestamp result
